│   Message:                                                                                       │
│     Form fields annotated with `Json[...]` around a sequence type (such as `Json[list[str]]`)    │
│ now read the raw string via `values.get()` instead of `getlist()`, so pydantic receives the JSON │
│ string rather than a list wrapping it.                                                           │
│                                                                                                  │
│     The change adds an `is_json_field` helper in `fastapi/_compat/v2.py` (exported from          │
│ `_compat/__init__.py`) that detects pydantic's `Json` metadata, and `_get_multidict_value` in    │
│ `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` now skips `getlist` for those fields. A manual `Json[list[str]]` │
│ form request parses correctly, and the existing form test files I ran (about 30 tests) pass.     │
│                                                                                                  │
│     I did not add a regression test. A `Json[dict]` form field still fails validation in my      │
│ manual check. That is a non-sequence path I didn't change, and I did not investigate it.         │
│ Pydantic v1 is out of scope, as the issue says. The patch is submitted (2762 bytes across 3      │
│ files).                                                                                          │
